                                "example_id": "2b9ed4bd-ffb9-4d87-adc9-590065c00e40",
                                "sense_id": "fcd102ce-e804-3d4d-adf4-eeef46fda260",
                                "text": "It was not, therefore, by an insolent usurpation that [Samuel Taylor] Coleridge persisted in monology through his whole life, but in virtue of a concession from the kindness and respect of his friends."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a86772d0-5392-4122-bfe7-3299f721fe91",
                                "sense_id": "fcd102ce-e804-3d4d-adf4-eeef46fda260",
                                "text": "Miriam would only speed up in her speech when she 'forgot' the presence of others, when she was, as it were, enveloped in monology."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3b04967f-0846-39b4-bcc7-a8e7ccdd43d8",
